{"id": "EUVD-2026-52603", "enisaUuid": "74c09d55-d2dc-3c54-91f8-c6e13d7b5cdb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: nVMX: Hide shadow VMCS right after VMCLEAR\n\nfree_nested() frees the shadow VMCS while vmcs01 still points to it. But\nbecause it is asynchronous with respect to loaded_vmcs_clear(), the vCPU\nmight migrate before the pointer is cleared and __loaded_vmcs_clear()\nmay then execute VMCLEAR.\n\nThe VMCS needs to stay attached until its explicit VMCLEAR completes, but\nthen it can be hidden and the page safely freed.", "datePublished": "2026-08-04T06:23:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:41", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b82c3144d8264265448292ca406f60bafeba3b6f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f50e6aec16f69627dbad5704d1e90a255d766a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc3eecfa219ebc9d01eaf7d1abd1441efe884dab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/af56298e9d86e6098cd1d2e155cb2949b7c45412", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/589419470030a89f16cf19300658b6dc644ca946", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8001d2ce9d9bd09118ce523aef595aa094573ae3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1dabef6e206568bf9d9ade74f6e56a48ea35695d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/622ebfac01ba4f9c0060cebd41257fe46fc4a0b3"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64562", "GHSA-mc77-r35g-cpmm"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06a2dc14-5e2a-3266-a5f7-e0f5fc89cb18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "355f4fb1405ec29d0fac49b4d41fcd78cbd455d5 <8001d2ce9d9bd09118ce523aef595aa094573ae3"}, {"id": "1c674e36-7001-3e99-bb16-818b2780f484", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.148"}, {"id": "30914096-72d0-319a-a125-fb124d4a69dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch